  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1138 PM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nCurrent high pressure over the region is progged to get a push\nnorth/northeast Saturday as now Hurricane Isaias moves onshore. \nLatest model solutions continue to keep Isaias east of the CWA, \nthough easterly winds and scattered cloud cover could move through\nnorthwest Arkansas Saturday. In the wake of the tropical system \nmoving farther north/northeast of the region, an additional ridge \nof high pressure is forecast to set up over the southern Plains. \nThis will likely continue the above seasonal average temperatures \nalong with breezy southerly winds Sunday into the first part of \nnext week. These conditions could create limited areas of fire \nweather concern over parts of northeast Oklahoma, where the higher\nwind gusts are anticipated. \n\nAlso over the weekend, an area of low pressure drops southeast\nalong the West Coast and merges with the remnants of tropical\nsystem Rachel. This low pressure system is then progged to move\nacross the Desert Southwest and into the southern/central Plains\nmid to latter part of next week. As this wave moves into the\nPlains, a cold front looks to approach the region, and the\ncombination of these features will increase the potential for\nshowers and thunderstorms to return to the CWA. Details with this\nwave will continue to be monitored and updated as it approaches.",
